      "reviewedAt": "2026-08-24T14:00:30Z",
      "note": "Reviewed both exploit-sequence receipts and call traces, the two pool creation traces, runtime bytecode at deployment and immediately before the exploit, the official post-mortem, and the commit-pinned reproduction. The selected transaction directly executes osETH/WETH pool 0xdacf5f...850c and wstETH/WETH pool 0x93d199...f0bd 133 and 117 times respectively. Their runtimes contain no DELEGATECALL, CALLCODE, or SELFDESTRUCT and retain deployment-to-pre-exploit hashes 0x72b6e1...ca441 and 0x070e56...c662f. Factory 0xdb8d75...1bd3a creates both pools via CREATE2 in the recorded deployment transactions. The exploit credits proceeds as Vault internal balance; 84 seconds later transaction 0xd15520...8569, sent by the same EOA to the attack contract created by the selected transaction, transfers exactly 6,587.440315017497938362 WETH, 6,851.122954235076557965 osETH, and 4,259.843451780587743322 wstETH from the Vault to attacker-controlled recipient 0xaa760d53541d8390074c61defeaba314675b8e3f."
